│ patch_description        │ This version switches from a heavily regularized, low-variance setup to a regime-aware,   │
│                          │ multi-scale feature stack with a more expressive XGBoost model.                           │
│                          │ The key change is to build only lagged/past-safe features from shifted price, volatility, │
│                          │ volume, and candle-shape data, then let a larger tree ensemble learn different behaviors  │
│                          │ across trending, mean-reverting, and volatile regimes.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Compared with the current implementation, this approach should improve directional        │
│                          │ accuracy by:                                                                              │
│                          │ - removing collapse-to-mean pressure from overly strong regularization,                   │
│                          │ - adding richer regime and momentum/mean-reversion signals,                               │
│                          │ - using past-only normalized features so the model can generalize better,                 │
│                          │ - increasing model capacity enough to produce a wider prediction distribution without     │
│                          │ overfitting aggressively.                                                                 │
