│ patch_description        │ The primary issue is extreme regularization preventing the model from expressing any      │
│                          │ signal (pred_std_ratio=0.0063). The collapse penalty dominates the score. I will:         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Drastically reduce regularization (reg_alpha → 0.001, reg_lambda → 0.1) to allow       │
│                          │ signal learning                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Increase learning_rate to 0.1 for faster convergence with fewer estimators             │
│                          │ 3. Reduce n_estimators to 200 to avoid overfitting with looser regularization             │
│                          │ 4. Adjust min_child_weight to 3 to allow finer splits capturing signal                    │
│                          │ 5. Add interaction features: ret_momentum (momentum of recent returns),                   │
│                          │ volatility-weighted returns, cross-regime features                                        │
│                          │ 6. Add decay-weighted momentum features that emphasize recent bars more                   │
│                          │ 7. Use less aggressive target clipping (98th percentile instead of 99th)                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This addresses the core constraint violation: regularization is so tight it's killing     │
│                          │ expressivity. The target accuracy of 0.52 is achievable - we just need the model to use   │
│                          │ the signal.                                                                               │
