╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ broader_signal_unclamp                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is still predicting too close to the mean, which is consistent with     │
│                          │ overly conservative tree growth and a feature set that is useful but not diverse enough   │
│                          │ to separate bullish vs bearish 15-minute regimes.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit makes two coordinated changes:                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Loosens the XGBoost regularization and increases model capacity slightly:              │
│                          │    - more trees, slightly deeper trees                                                    │
│                          │    - lower `min_child_weight`, `reg_alpha`, `reg_lambda`                                  │
│                          │    - lower learning rate to stabilize the extra capacity                                  │
│                          │    - slightly more aggressive clipping (`CLIP_PERCENTILE=99`) so the model can see a      │
│                          │ wider target range                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Expands `build_features()` with short-horizon regime-sensitive signals that are still  │
│                          │ causal:                                                                                   │
│                          │    - fast/medium return momentum                                                          │
│                          │    - return spread and acceleration                                                       │
│                          │    - rolling z-score of returns                                                           │
│                          │    - volume z-score and volume change                                                     │
│                          │    - range expansion and candle body/wick structure                                       │
│                          │    - price position inside recent high/low range                                          │
│                          │    - trend vs mean-reversion interaction using short-vs-long momentum                     │
│                          │    - a volatility-adjusted momentum feature                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These additions are designed to improve directional separation without blowing up feature │
│                          │ count or introducing lookahead. The feature total remains comfortably below 80.           │
