│ patch_description        │ The current model suffers from a severe 'prediction collapse' (pred_std_ratio < 0.01),    │
│                          │ where it predicts values too close to the mean, resulting in heavy penalties. This is     │
│                          │ caused by overly conservative hyperparameters (low depth, high min_child_weight, very low │
│                          │ learning rate) and a sparse feature set.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I am proposing to:                                                                        │
│                          │ 1. Increase model expressivity by increasing `max_depth` to 6, decreasing                 │
│                          │ `min_child_weight` to 2, and increasing the `learning_rate` to 0.05. This forces the      │
│                          │ model to capture more granular signals.                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Restore and expand the feature set to include mean-reversion indicators (SMA           │
│                          │ deviations), momentum-volatility interactions, and price positioning within recent        │
│                          │ ranges. These features provide the necessary signal for the model to differentiate        │
│                          │ between market regimes and generate more varied predictions.                              │
│                          │ 3. Increase `n_estimators` and `early_stopping_rounds` to allow the more complex model    │
│                          │ sufficient time to converge.                                                              │
