│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_stack_xgb                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ I took inspiration from the existing program’s emphasis on classic technical indicators,  │
│                          │ volatility, volume, and regime awareness, but replaced the mostly low-signal, heavily     │
│                          │ regularized setup with a more expressive “regime stack” feature design.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new approach builds a compact set of past-only features that are explicitly organized │
│                          │ around:                                                                                   │
│                          │ - multi-horizon momentum and mean-reversion tension,                                      │
│                          │ - volatility compression/expansion,                                                       │
│                          │ - candle anatomy and range efficiency,                                                    │
│                          │ - robust rolling normalization using only prior bars,                                     │
│                          │ - regime-conditioned interactions between trend, volatility, and volume,                  │
│                          │ - optional orderbook/funding signals transformed into stable imbalance and surprise       │
│                          │ measures.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Compared with the original, this version avoids relying on a few raw indicators and       │
│                          │ instead creates a broader but still controlled feature space that helps XGBoost detect    │
│                          │ when short-term directional edges are more likely to flip or persist. I also loosened     │
│                          │ regularization and increased tree capacity so the model is less likely to collapse toward │
│                          │ the mean, which should raise predicted dispersion while keeping the feature count under   │
│                          │ the limit.                                                                                │
