│                          │ 2. Increase learning_rate (0.05→0.08) for faster convergence                              │
│                          │ 3. Reduce gamma (0.5→0.1) to allow more tree splits                                       │
│                          │ 4. Add binary regime indicator features (momentum_positive, vol_high_binary,              │
│                          │ trend_up/down, momentum_strong, etc.) that create natural decision boundaries and help    │
│                          │ trees learn regime-specific patterns                                                      │
│                          │ 5. Increase n_estimators slightly (600→750) to compensate for lower regularization        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The binary features act as "regime gates" that allow XGBoost to learn different           │
│                          │ directional patterns in different market conditions, dramatically improving               │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio while maintaining validation DA.                                           │
