│ patch_name               │ increase_expressivity_and_add_microstructure                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The previous model showed good directional accuracy (0.53+) but suffered from a           │
│                          │ significant "collapse" penalty, meaning the predictions were too clustered around the     │
│                          │ mean. To address this, I am:                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Increasing model expressivity by increasing `max_depth` to 7 and `n_estimators` to     │
│                          │ 1000, while reducing `reg_lambda` and `reg_alpha` to allow the model to capture more      │
│                          │ granular signals.                                                                         │
│                          │ 2. Adjusting `CLIP_PERCENTILE` to 98 to preserve more target variance, which provides     │
│                          │ stronger gradients for the model to learn from and encourages higher prediction           │
│                          │ dispersion.                                                                               │
│                          │ 3. Adding several high-value features:                                                    │
│                          │    - `dist_ema_200`: Long-term trend deviation.                                           │
│                          │    - `vpt_20`: Volume-Price Trend to capture liquidity-driven moves.                      │
│                          │    - `vol_skew_30`: Rolling skewness of returns to identify asymmetric risk regimes.      │
│                          │    - `vol_shock_5_20`: Short-term volatility spikes relative to the medium-term.          │
│                          │    - `ny_session`: A binary indicator for the high-volatility US trading window.          │
│                          │    - `volume_z_60`: Z-scored volume over a longer lookback to identify significant flow.  │
│                          │ These changes aim to push the `pred_std_ratio` closer to the 0.15 target while            │
│                          │ maintaining or improving DA.                                                              │
