╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_lagged_expansion                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is still collapsing toward the mean, which usually means the trees are  │
│                          │ too constrained and the feature space does not provide enough separable structure. I      │
│                          │ would address this in two complementary ways:                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Loosen the XGBoost bias slightly:                                                      │
│                          │    - reduce `min_child_weight` and regularization,                                        │
│                          │    - increase tree count a bit,                                                           │
│                          │    - use a slightly higher learning rate with more expressive trees.                      │
│                          │    This should increase prediction variance without pushing into heavy overfit, since the │
│                          │ current train/val gap is small.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Add a small set of regime-conditioned lagged features:                                 │
│                          │    - short-horizon return and volatility ratios,                                          │
│                          │    - volatility-adjusted momentum,                                                        │
│                          │    - trend slope proxy,                                                                   │
│                          │    - rolling correlation between volume and returns,                                      │
│                          │    - candlestick body/wick structure,                                                     │
│                          │    - normalized mean-reversion distance and range position.                               │
│                          │    These are all past-only and help the model distinguish when momentum vs reversion is   │
│                          │ more likely. The feature count remains comfortably below the 80-feature limit.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I am also slightly tightening the target clipping from 99 to 98.5 to reduce extreme-label │
│                          │ noise while keeping enough signal.                                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0190                                                                                   │
