│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ expressive_regime_boost                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The previous model suffered from "prediction collapse," meaning it was too conservative   │
│                          │ and its predicted standard deviation was far below the actual market standard deviation.  │
│                          │ To fix this, I am:                                                                        │
│                          │ 1. Increasing model expressivity by increasing `max_depth` (8) and `learning_rate`        │
│                          │ (0.08), and significantly lowering the `reg_lambda` regularization (0.01).                │
│                          │ 2. Implementing a strict "shift-by-1" feature engineering pipeline to ensure 100%         │
│                          │ compliance with the "use only past data" constraint, which also helps stabilize           │
│                          │ directional signals.                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Adding a broader set of features including Parkinson volatility (high-low range        │
│                          │ measure), market efficiency ratios, and volume z-scores to provide clearer                │
│                          │ signal-to-noise.                                                                          │
│                          │ 4. Setting `CLIP_PERCENTILE` to 99.0 to allow the model to learn from a wider             │
│                          │ distribution of returns, reducing the incentive for the model to "hide" at the mean.      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
