                        Patch Metadata - Gen 33/100 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regimexgb_pastshift                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a fairly deep XGBoost model with strong regularization and a     │
│                          │ feature set that is mostly price/volume trend indicators. The main weakness shown by the  │
│                          │ metrics is prediction collapse: `pred_std_ratio` stays very low, so the model is too      │
│                          │ conservative and produces outputs close to the mean.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ My redesign changes two things:                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Feature engineering becomes past-shifted and more regime-aware**                     │
│                          │    - All raw inputs are shifted by 1 bar before any transformation to strictly avoid      │
│                          │ lookahead.                                                                                │
│                          │    - I add multi-scale momentum, volatility, candle-structure, volume-pressure, and       │
│                          │ regime-interaction features.                                                              │
│                          │    - I keep the total feature count under 80.                                             │
│                          │    - I emphasize short-horizon directional structure and regime conditioning, which       │
│                          │ should help reduce mean collapse and improve directional accuracy on shifting crypto      │
│                          │ regimes.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **XGBoost is made more expressive but less over-constrained**                          │
│                          │    - Lower depth than the current overly complex setup, but more trees and a smaller      │
│                          │ learning rate for smoother generalization.                                                │
│                          │    - Reduced regularization relative to the collapsing models, with slightly higher       │
│                          │ subsampling and column sampling to preserve signal diversity.                             │
│                          │    - Lower `min_child_weight` and slightly more trees should increase prediction variance │
│                          │ without causing a large overfit gap.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also lower target clipping slightly so the model sees more of the directional tail      │
│                          │ behavior, while still being robust to outliers.                                           │
