│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ feature_diversity_and_params                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The previous model is suffering from a significant "prediction collapse" (pred_std_ratio  │
│                          │ = 0.04, well below the target 0.15), meaning it is essentially predicting the mean return │
│                          │ due to a low signal-to-noise ratio in the provided features. To combat this, I am:        │
│                          │ 1. Refining the feature set to include 'Efficiency Ratio' (to distinguish trend from      │
│                          │ noise), 'BB Width' (to capture volatility clusters), and 'Range Stretch' (to identify     │
│                          │ overextended price action).                                                               │
│                          │ 2. Adjusting hyperparameters: lowering 'max_depth' to 7 to improve generalization (deep   │
│                          │ trees often fit noise in 15m bars) and slowing the 'learning_rate' while increasing the   │
│                          │ number of estimators and patience. This encourages the model to find subtle directional   │
│                          │ signals that are otherwise lost in MSE optimization.                                      │
│                          │ 3. Increasing 'CLIP_PERCENTILE' to 99 to preserve more target variance, which can help    │
│                          │ the model distinguish between meaningful moves and noise.                                 │
│                          │ 4. Adding interactions between volume, volatility, and price direction to provide more    │
│                          │ 'expressivity' to the trees.                                                              │
