│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ expressivity_and_flow_indicators                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The previous model suffered from a significant 'collapse toward mean' (pred_std_ratio of  │
│                          │ ~0.036 where 0.15 is required). This suggests the model is finding the noise-to-signal    │
│                          │ ratio too high and defaulting to safe, near-zero predictions.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To address this, I am:                                                                    │
│                          │ 1. Refining XGBoost hyperparameters: Increasing 'n_estimators' to 1000 and lowering       │
│                          │ 'learning_rate' to 0.03. This slower learning process with more steps typically allows    │
│                          │ the model to build a more robust signal in financial time-series data compared to the     │
│                          │ faster LR=0.1. I also set 'max_depth' to 7 and 'min_child_weight' to 2 to maintain        │
│                          │ expressivity while preventing capture of single-outlier noise.                            │
│                          │ 2. Adding 'Energy and Flow' indicators: Money Flow Index (MFI) and Chaikin Money Flow     │
│                          │ (CMF) proxies are added to capture volume-weighted price pressure, which is often more    │
│                          │ predictive than price alone in crypto perps.                                              │
│                          │ 3. Adding Keltner Channel and Williams %R indicators: These provide better context for    │
│                          │ overbought/oversold regimes relative to volatility than basic RSI or Bollinger Bands.     │
│                          │ 4. Adding interaction terms: Specifically crossing volume dynamics with momentum (RSI) to │
│                          │ identify high-conviction moves.                                                           │
