│ patch_description        │ The current model's performance drop (from -0.15 to -0.57) is primarily due to an extra   │
│                          │ `shift(1)` applied to the base OHLCV series, which makes the features 1-bar stale         │
│                          │ relative to the target. I am reverting this shift to align with the successful prior      │
│                          │ programs.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the model is suffering from "prediction collapse" (pred_std_ratio = 0.01),  │
│                          │ meaning it is underfitting and predicting the mean. I am increasing model expressivity    │
│                          │ by:                                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Increasing `max_depth` and `learning_rate`.                                            │
│                          │ 2. Reducing `reg_lambda` to allow the model to capture more signal.                       │
│                          │ 3. Adding high-signal features like `vol_cv_20`, `dist_h_100`, and `force_index_7`.       │
│                          │ 4. Removing redundant feature definitions and the arbitrary `iloc[:, :80]` cap to ensure  │
│                          │ all signal-carrying features (like funding and orderbook) are preserved.                  │
