│ patch_description        │ The current model suffers from a significant 'prediction collapse' (pred_std_ratio =      │
│                          │ 0.04), meaning it is underfitting the variance of the target returns. To address this, I  │
│                          │ am increasing the model's expressivity by:                                                │
│                          │ 1. Increasing `max_depth` from 5 to 7 and decreasing `min_child_weight` from 3 to 1 to    │
│                          │ allow the trees to capture more granular patterns.                                        │
│                          │ 2. Reducing `reg_lambda` from 0.6 to 0.1 to loosen the L2 penalty on leaf weights.        │
│                          │ 3. Increasing `learning_rate` to 0.05 to allow the model to learn faster and produce more │
│                          │ distinct predictions.                                                                     │
│                          │ 4. Adding high-signal features: Rolling Autocorrelation (to capture                       │
│                          │ momentum/mean-reversion persistence), Efficiency Ratio (to distinguish between trending   │
│                          │ and range-bound markets), and Volatility Shocks.                                          │
│                          │ 5. Pruning redundant lags to stay within the 80-feature limit and avoid the curse of      │
│                          │ dimensionality.                                                                           │
