│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ increase_expressivity_and_signal                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current model suffers from "collapsed predictions" (pred_std_ratio = 0.009), meaning  │
│                          │ it is too conservative and predicts values very close to the mean. To fix this, I am:     │
│                          │ 1. Increasing model expressivity: Increasing `max_depth` (4 -> 6), decreasing             │
│                          │ `min_child_weight` (10 -> 1), and increasing `learning_rate` (0.01 -> 0.05).              │
│                          │ 2. Reducing regularization: Lowering `reg_lambda` and `reg_alpha` to allow the model to   │
│                          │ fit the signal more closely.                                                              │
│                          │ 3. Enhancing features: Adding multi-horizon log-returns, rolling Z-scores for returns and │
│                          │ volume, and candle anatomy features (wick/body ratios).                                   │
│                          │ 4. Strict Past-Data Compliance: Ensuring all features derived from OHLCV are explicitly   │
│                          │ shifted by at least 1 bar to prevent any lookahead and comply with constraints.           │
│                          │ 5. Outlier Robustness: Adjusting `CLIP_PERCENTILE` to 98.0 to reduce the influence of     │
│                          │ extreme tails on the RMSE objective, which often causes the model to bias towards the     │
│                          │ mean.                                                                                     │
