│ patch_name               │ regime_boosted_features                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This edit aims to reduce prediction collapse by adding a small set of higher-signal,      │
│                          │ regime-aware features while keeping the feature count under the 80-feature cap. The       │
│                          │ current feature set is already decent on DA but still too mean-reverting in prediction    │
│                          │ space (`pred_std_ratio` is low). To address that, I’m adding:                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - shorter-horizon return acceleration and trend persistence features                      │
│                          │ - normalized breakout / compression indicators                                            │
│                          │ - a couple of regime interaction terms that let XGBoost separate trend-following from     │
│                          │ mean-reversion conditions more cleanly                                                    │
│                          │ - a lightweight “intrabar position vs volatility” feature that often helps perpetual      │
│                          │ futures on 15m bars                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All of these are past-only and explicitly shifted where needed. This should give the      │
│                          │ model more expressive separation without violating the no-lookahead constraint. I also    │
│                          │ leave the feature count safely below 80 by slightly trimming redundant windows.           │
