│ patch_description        │ Optimized the model for higher expressivity and signal extraction to address the          │
│                          │ prediction collapse.                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Increased expressivity: Increased `max_depth` to 7, reduced `reg_lambda` to 0.1, and   │
│                          │ decreased `min_child_weight` to 2. This pushes the model away from predicting the mean    │
│                          │ and toward capturing tail-end directional signals.                                        │
│                          │ 2. Robust feature engineering: Implemented a strictly past-only feature set by ensuring   │
│                          │ every calculation is shifted by at least one bar (using `shift(1)`).                      │
│                          │ 3. Signal refinement: Added classic technical indicators like RSI and normalized distance │
│                          │ from high/low to capture mean reversion.                                                  │
│                          │ 4. Feature pruning: Consolidated features to approximately 55 high-signal inputs (under   │
│                          │ the 80-feature limit) to focus on multi-horizon momentum, volatility regimes, and         │
│                          │ volume-confirmed moves while avoiding dimensionality issues.                              │
│                          │ 5. Orderbook and Funding: Maintained focus on market microstructure cues (OBI and         │
│                          │ funding) which often provide the cleanest alpha in perp markets.                          │
