│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ increase_expressivity_and_vol_features                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The model currently suffers from a "collapse toward the mean" (pred_std_ratio ~0.06),     │
│                          │ which limits its performance despite decent directional accuracy. To address this, I am   │
│                          │ increasing model expressivity by:                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Tuning hyperparameters: Higher `max_depth`, lower `min_child_weight`, and reduced      │
│                          │ `reg_lambda` to allow the model to capture more granular signals.                         │
│                          │ 2. Adjusting `CLIP_PERCENTILE` to 97 to slightly reduce the influence of extreme bps      │
│                          │ outliers which can dampen the gradient for typical bars.                                  │
│                          │ 3. Adding "Amihud Illiquidity" (price change per volume) and "Volatility of Volatility"   │
│                          │ features to help the model distinguish between noisy churn and high-conviction moves.     │
│                          │ 4. Adding price-distance features normalized by ATR to better capture overextended        │
│                          │ regimes.                                                                                  │
