│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ expressive_regime_features                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is still showing mean-collapsed predictions (`pred_std_ratio` ~ 0.04)   │
│                          │ despite decent DA, which suggests it is under-utilizing the available signal. The safest  │
│                          │ next step is to increase tree expressivity a bit and add a small set of regime-sensitive  │
│                          │ features that are still strictly past-only.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I am proposing:                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Looser XGBoost regularization and slightly deeper trees to let the model separate      │
│                          │ regimes more effectively.                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Additional short-horizon, volatility-normalized, and quantile-style features that      │
│                          │ often help BTC/ETH/SOL perp directionality at 15m:                                        │
│                          │    - short-horizon acceleration and slope                                                 │
│                          │    - rolling rank / breakout context                                                      │
│                          │    - realized volatility change                                                           │
│                          │    - volume shock and trend/vol interactions                                              │
│                          │    - orderbook and funding regime interactions                                            │
│                          │ 3. Keep total feature count under 80 by explicitly selecting a compact subset of the      │
│                          │ strongest features rather than blindly truncating.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve prediction dispersion without materially increasing overfit, and it   │
│                          │ targets the main failure mode seen in the metrics.                                        │
