│ patch_name               │ capacity_boost_and_lagged_signals                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The previous model suffered from a significant prediction collapse (pred_std_ratio =      │
│                          │ 0.027), indicating it was underfitting the variance of the target. To counter this, I am  │
│                          │ dramatically increasing the model capacity by raising n_estimators and max_depth, while   │
│                          │ simultaneously lowering the learning rate to ensure stable convergence. I also increased  │
│                          │ CLIP_PERCENTILE to 98th percentile to retain more tail signals.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the feature engineering side, I've added:                                              │
│                          │ 1. Autoregressive features: Lagged returns (t-1, t-2) to capture short-term momentum or   │
│                          │ mean-reversion persistence.                                                               │
│                          │ 2. Distributional features: Rolling skewness (24h) to identify asymmetrical risk regimes. │
│                          │ 3. Lagged exogenous features: Lagged Order Book Imbalance (OBI) and Funding Rate to       │
│                          │ better capture lead-lag relationships which are often present in perp futures.            │
│                          │ These additions stay within the 80-feature limit while providing the model with more      │
│                          │ context to avoid simply predicting the mean.                                              │
