│ patch_description        │ The current model is still collapsing toward the mean, which usually means the tree       │
│                          │ ensemble is too constrained relative to the signal in 15-minute perp returns. I’m         │
│                          │ proposing two coordinated changes:                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Loosen XGBoost regularization and increase tree budget slightly so the model can       │
│                          │ express sharper directional edges without over-smoothing.                                 │
│                          │    - Reduce `min_child_weight`, `reg_alpha`, and `reg_lambda`                             │
│                          │    - Use a slightly higher learning rate with more trees                                  │
│                          │    - Add `gamma=0` explicitly to avoid unnecessary split suppression                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Expand the feature set with a compact regime-aware stack:                              │
│                          │    - Short/medium EMA gaps and slope features                                             │
│                          │    - ATR-normalized impulse / trend efficiency                                            │
│                          │    - A simple ADX-like directional strength proxy                                         │
│                          │    - Longer range-position context                                                        │
│                          │    - A few cross-regime interactions that help the model behave differently in trend vs   │
│                          │ chop                                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help increase `pred_std_ratio` while keeping feature count comfortably below  │
│                          │ the limit and avoiding any lookahead.                                                     │
