                        Patch Metadata - Gen 71/100 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ aggressive_deregularization_with_signal_boost                                             │
│ patch_description        │ **Key Analysis of Current Performance:**                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program achieves val_DA=0.5226 and pred_std_ratio=0.0607, indicating          │
│                          │ prediction collapse toward the mean. All six previous iterations show the same symptom:   │
│                          │ the model is being over-regularized, suppressing prediction variance to only ~6% of       │
│                          │ actual variance. The collapse penalty consistently dominates the score (0.447–0.681       │
│                          │ across iterations).                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Root Cause:**                                                                           │
│                          │ - Regularization is too aggressive (reg_lambda, reg_alpha, min_child_weight all           │
│                          │ constraining tree growth)                                                                 │
│                          │ - Learning rate is too conservative (0.03) combined with high L2 regularization           │
│                          │ - Feature engineering is sophisticated but the model cannot express the learned patterns  │
│                          │ due to regularization choking the output                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **New Strategy:**                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Dramatically reduce L2/L1 regularization** (reg_lambda: 0.35→0.02, reg_alpha:        │
│                          │ 0.02→0.0)                                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. **Increase tree depth and leaf expressivity** (max_depth: 5→7, min_child_weight: 3→1)  │
│                          │ 3. **Boost learning rate** (0.03→0.08) to escape underfitting                             │
│                          │ 4. **Increase estimators moderately** (850→1100) to allow more complex ensemble patterns  │
│                          │ 5. **Relax subsampling** (0.82→0.9) to give trees more data to learn from                 │
│                          │ 6. **Add signal-amplifying features** (momentum z-scores, volatility-adjusted returns,    │
│                          │ interaction compression)                                                                  │
