│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_overregularization_and_curate_features                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is severely over-regularized (reg_lambda=0.8, lr=0.015) which causes    │
│                          │ prediction collapse. Prior experiments show that models with reg_lambda=0.05-0.15 and     │
│                          │ lr=0.05-0.10 achieve better val_DA (0.52-0.53).                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will:                                                                                   │
│                          │ 1. Increase learning_rate from 0.015 to 0.08 (closest to best historical performance)     │
│                          │ 2. Reduce reg_lambda from 0.8 to 0.12 (balanced regularization)                           │
│                          │ 3. Reduce min_child_weight from 5 to 2 (allow more flexible tree fitting)                 │
│                          │ 4. Reduce n_estimators from 1400 to 900 (avoid overfitting with lighter trees)            │
│                          │ 5. Curate features: Remove redundant lagged features (ret_1_lag1, ret_1_lag2, obi_lag1,   │
│                          │ funding_lag1) and low-signal skew feature. Keep only essential interaction and regime     │
│                          │ features.                                                                                 │
│                          │ 6. Keep max_depth=6 (good balance) and increase subsample/colsample to 0.9 (regularize    │
│                          │ via sampling, not via penalty)                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This mirrors the best-performing prior config (score -0.20) which had val_DA=0.5226 and   │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio=0.0607.                                                                    │
