│ patch_description        │ This edit implements aggressive feature pruning combined with stronger regularization to  │
│                          │ combat prediction collapse. The strategy:                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reduce feature count from 60+ to ~35**: Keep only the most orthogonal, non-redundant │
│                          │ features. Remove:                                                                         │
│                          │    - Redundant momentum acceleration features (keep only ret_accel_12_6)                  │
│                          │    - Duplicate regime interactions (keep only core vol_regime and trend interactions)     │
│                          │    - Weak binary regime signals that don't add orthogonal information                     │
│                          │    - Redundant RSI variants                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Strengthen regularization**: Increase reg_alpha to 0.01 (L1 penalty) to force        │
│                          │ feature selection, and reg_lambda to 0.03 to prevent overfitting. This combination helps  │
│                          │ the model learn which features truly matter.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Adjust hyperparameters for smaller feature set**:                                    │
│                          │    - Reduce max_depth from 7 to 5 (smaller trees fit smaller feature sets better)         │
│                          │    - Reduce n_estimators from 1000 to 600 (fewer trees prevent overfitting with strong    │
│                          │ regularization)                                                                           │
│                          │    - Increase learning_rate from 0.06 to 0.08 (compensate for fewer estimators)           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Loosen clipping slightly**: CLIP_PERCENTILE from 98→97 to keep more gradient signal  │
│                          │ while still limiting extreme outliers.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale: With fewer, cleaner features and stronger regularization, the model will   │
│                          │ make more confident predictions on the signals that matter, improving pred_std_ratio      │
│                          │ while maintaining validation accuracy.                                                    │
