│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ higher_signal_regime_features                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current model is heavily underconfident (`pred_std_ratio` is far below target), which │
│                          │ usually means the tree ensemble is too constrained and the feature set is not providing   │
│                          │ enough separable regime information. I’m proposing two coordinated changes:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Relax XGBoost regularization and give it more capacity to fit weak but real            │
│                          │ directional edges:                                                                        │
│                          │    - more trees,                                                                          │
│                          │    - slightly deeper trees,                                                               │
│                          │    - lower `min_child_weight`,                                                            │
│                          │    - lower `reg_lambda`,                                                                  │
│                          │    - a bit more subsampling to retain robustness,                                         │
│                          │    - slightly smaller learning rate with more rounds.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Add a small set of high-value past-only features that improve regime discrimination    │
│                          │ without exploding dimensionality:                                                         │
│                          │    - normalized lagged returns and return spreads,                                        │
│                          │    - short-horizon realized volatility shifts,                                            │
│                          │    - EMA-based trend spread,                                                              │
│                          │    - VWAP-distance z-score,                                                               │
│                          │    - RSI slope / midline state,                                                           │
│                          │    - volume shock / price-volume interaction,                                             │
│                          │    - a short regime persistence measure.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These features are designed to help the model separate trend, mean-reversion, and         │
│                          │ volatility-expansion periods, which should improve directional accuracy while also        │
│                          │ increasing prediction dispersion away from the mean.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 8                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0304                                                                                   │
