│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ btc_15m_regimeboost                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program is dominated by a fairly regularized XGBoost model with a broad but   │
│                          │ still mostly linear feature set, which is why prediction dispersion stays low and the     │
│                          │ model keeps collapsing toward the mean. The key tunable parameters are `learning_rate`,   │
│                          │ `n_estimators`, `max_depth`, `min_child_weight`, `reg_alpha`, `reg_lambda`, `subsample`,  │
│                          │ `colsample_bytree`, `gamma`, `CLIP_PERCENTILE`, and `MIN_PRED_STD_RATIO`.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ My rewrite increases useful expressivity while keeping overfit controlled:                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - **More responsive boosting**: slightly lower `learning_rate`, more trees, and a bit     │
│                          │ deeper depth to let the model form stronger directional partitions.                       │
│                          │ - **Less shrinkage on signal**: reduced `reg_lambda` and `gamma`, with modest             │
│                          │ `reg_alpha`, to avoid mean-collapse.                                                      │
│                          │ - **Regime-aware feature set**: adds short/medium momentum, volatility                    │
│                          │ compression/expansion, trend strength, candle anatomy, volume shocks, funding dynamics,   │
│                          │ and interaction terms that are all computed strictly from past data.                      │
│                          │ - **More robust normalization**: uses rolling z-scores and robust ratios to make          │
│                          │ BTC/ETH/SOL perps more comparable across volatility regimes.                              │
│                          │ - **Better clipping balance**: slightly relaxes target clipping so large directional bars │
│                          │ still contribute to gradients.                                                            │
│                          │ - **Dispersion floor**: raises the effective dispersion target a bit so the model is      │
│                          │ nudged away from flat predictions.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result should increase `pred_std_ratio` while preserving or improving validation DA   │
│                          │ by making the trees split on regime-conditioned directional structure instead of          │
│                          │ averaging it away.                                                                        │
