│ patch_description        │ This update aims to fix the current “prediction collapse” symptom by making the tree      │
│                          │ ensemble a bit more expressive while keeping regularization moderate. The main issue in   │
│                          │ the latest results is that `pred_std_ratio` is still low, which means the model is too    │
│                          │ conservative and not separating bullish/bearish cases enough.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the feature side, I’m adding a compact set of strictly past-only, lagged               │
│                          │ regime/momentum features. These are designed to help XGBoost learn when trend-following   │
│                          │ vs mean-reversion behavior is more likely, especially across changing volatility          │
│                          │ conditions. I also shift the orderbook/funding inputs by one bar to make the past-only    │
│                          │ constraint explicit and to reduce any chance of same-bar leakage.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature count remains comfortably below 80, and the added calculations are            │
│                          │ lightweight enough to stay within runtime limits.                                         │
