│ patch_name               │ increase_expressivity_and_prune                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The model is currently suffering from prediction collapse (pred_std_ratio = 0.06),        │
│                          │ indicating it is too conservative. To address this, I am increasing model expressivity by │
│                          │ raising the learning rate to 0.1, increasing max_depth to 6, and significantly reducing   │
│                          │ reg_lambda to 0.01.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the feature engineering side, I am pruning several redundant or less impactful         │
│                          │ features (ret_24, vol_192, rsi_28, volume_chg_8, range_pos_60, range_width_60,            │
│                          │ momentum_slow, obi_lag1) to stay within the 80-feature limit. I am introducing three      │
│                          │ high-signal features:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Efficiency Ratio (Kaufman's ER): To distinguish between trending and noisy market      │
│                          │ states.                                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Range Relative: To identify volatility breakouts relative to recent history.           │
│                          │ 3. Volume Price Impulse: To capture momentum confirmed by volume surges.                  │
